OrionLayer open fix 64 — the Races screen's spies and missions, set by a client
================================================================================

Work order 197 (Part B; 196's parked E1, decided B-3). orion2re 9e19c9f3 on
`orionlayer-local`, on top of 76c7b880 (open fix 65). src/ext only.

WHAT IS MISSING. On the Races screen (SCREEN_RACE) the player moves spies
between the races' groups and the agent pool by picking icons up with the
mouse and dropping them, and sets each race's mission with its buttons;
nothing of it is a field a client can activate, so an HD Races screen could
show the spies but not move them.

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS. MSG_SET_SPIES (0x89): uint8 n, then n x (uint8 player,
uint8 spies, uint8 mission — 1 to 3, or 0 to keep it), then uint8 the agent
pool. The Tick applies it only on SCREEN_RACE with nothing held in the
mouse's group, only when every race the screen lists is named once, each
count is at most 63, and the total equals the screen's own total — all or
nothing. It writes the screen's icon groups, calls the game's own
Calculate_Icon_Group_Data_, and sets the player record through the same
BILL setters the screen's RETURN uses (spies, missions, the agent pool).

BEHAVIOUR WITHOUT ORIONLAYER: unchanged. Nothing runs unless a client sends
the message.

HOW TO REVERT. git revert 9e19c9f3.

